1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,435
This morning, half of his house was missing.

2
00:00:03,685 --> 00:00:08,551
Not broken. Not burned. Just... gone. Like someone forgot to draw it.

3
00:00:09,001 --> 00:00:12,168
Then the sky opened... and a pen came down.

4
00:00:12,318 --> 00:00:17,216
A giant pen. It started drawing his house back, line by line.

5
00:00:17,566 --> 00:00:20,532
But the lines came out thin. And grey.

6
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:25,319
Then the pen coughed... and dropped a single drop of ink at his feet.

7
00:00:25,969 --> 00:00:29,401
Through its side, he could see the ink left inside.

8
00:00:29,651 --> 00:00:32,573
Almost none. The pen was running out.

9
00:00:38,623 --> 00:00:41,922
Everything in his world had been drawn by that pen.

10
00:00:42,172 --> 00:00:45,756
Every tree. Every cloud. Every brick. Even him.

11
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:50,576
And whatever it couldn't redraw by morning... faded away for good.

12
00:00:51,126 --> 00:00:52,649
So he made a plan.

13
00:00:52,799 --> 00:00:58,160
Every drop the pen spilled, he would catch. And one day, he would give it all back.

14
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:03,691
On day three, the trees faded. He caught four drops.

15
00:01:05,841 --> 00:01:10,243
On day eight, the clouds were gone. So was the house next door.

16
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:16,747
Day fifteen. No more colour. The road was just one line.

17
00:01:18,897 --> 00:01:24,605
Day twenty-two. The sun was only an outline. But the jar was almost full.

18
00:01:26,855 --> 00:01:30,485
He told himself everything was going to be okay.

19
00:01:32,835 --> 00:01:38,578
On day twenty-nine, the pen came down again. But this time, it was upside down.

20
00:01:38,828 --> 00:01:41,316
It wasn't drawing. It was erasing.

21
00:01:41,566 --> 00:01:46,118
His house lifted off the page, line by line... and flew away.

22
00:01:46,468 --> 00:01:49,171
He chased the lines to the edge of the paper.

23
00:01:49,721 --> 00:01:53,114
And on the other side... was a brand new page.

24
00:01:53,364 --> 00:01:57,581
New trees. New clouds. Bright colours. And a new stickman.

25
00:01:58,331 --> 00:02:00,974
The pen was never running out of ink.

26
00:02:01,324 --> 00:02:02,931
It was taking it back.

27
00:02:03,481 --> 00:02:08,677
That missing half of his house wasn't an accident. It was the first thing it took.

28
00:02:10,627 --> 00:02:15,144
Now his page was empty. Just him... and one jar of ink.

29
00:02:15,494 --> 00:02:17,561
The eraser turned toward him.

30
00:02:18,111 --> 00:02:22,648
He dipped his finger in the jar, and drew the only thing that mattered.

31
00:02:22,898 --> 00:02:23,949
A door.

32
00:02:27,599 --> 00:02:32,261
On the new page, there was now a stickman who wasn't supposed to be there.

33
00:02:32,811 --> 00:02:34,725
And the pen... had noticed.
